{{for|the American actress|Billie Burke}} {{Infobox person | name = Billy Burke | image = | caption = | birth_name = William Albert Burke | birth_date = {{Birth date and age|1966|11|25|mf=y}} | birth_place = [[Bellingham]], Washington, US | occupation = Musician, Film actor | years_active = 1990–present }} '''William Albert "Billy" Burke''' (born November 25, 1966) is an American actor. He is known for his role as [[List of Twilight characters#Charlie Swan|Charlie Swan]] in ''[[Twilight (2008 film)|Twilight]]'', ''[[The Twilight Saga: New Moon]]'' and the 2010 film ''[[The Twilight Saga: Eclipse]]''. He is also known for his role as [[Gary Matheson]] in the second season of ''[[24 (TV series)|24]]''.
==Life and career== Burke was born in [[Bellingham]], Washington. His television credits include roles in ''[[Star Trek: Deep Space Nine]]'' (in the episode "[[Second Skin (DS9 episode)|Second Skin]]"), ''[[Party of Five]]'', ''[[Gilmore Girls]]'', ''[[Karen Sisco]]'', ''[[Fringe (TV series)|Fringe]]'', ''[[Monk (TV series)|Monk]]'' and ''[[The Closer]]'' (Season 4, episode 13, "[[Power of Attorney]]" playing the attorney Phillip Stroh). He also plays Detective Eric Box in the movie ''[[Untraceable]]''.
His motion picture credits include ''[[Jane Austen's Mafia!]]'', ''[[Along Came a Spider]]'', ''[[Final Jeopardy (2001 film)|Final Jeopardy]]'', ''[[Flashpoint (TV series)|Flashpoint]]'' and ''[[Ladder 49]]''. His upcoming film credits include [[The Fallen (film)|''The Fallen'']], ''[[Forfeit (film)|Forfeit]]'', ''[[Fracture (2007 film)|Fracture]]'' and ''[[Retirement (film)|Retirement]]''. He also appeared in ''[[Feast of Love]]'' (2007), co-starring [[Selma Blair]] and [[Morgan Freeman]]. In 2008, Burke appeared in ''[[Twilight (2008 film)|Twilight]]'', based on the best-selling novel by [[Stephenie Meyer]], playing the role of [[Charlie Swan (Twilight)|Charlie Swan]].<ref>[http://www.creators.com/lifestylefeatures/hollywood-exclusive/tyson-beckford-enjoying-men-s-supermodel-success-reno-911-s-lennon-delivers-the-state-of-the-state.html Tyson Beckford Enjoying Men's "Supermodel" Success/"Reno 911's Lennon Delivers the State of the State by Marilyn Beck & Stacy Jenel Smith on Creators.com – A Syndicate Of Talent<!-- Bot generated title -->]</ref> He also portrayed Bobby's brother Jack on the show ''[[My Boys]]''. Burke reprised his role as Charlie Swan in ''Twilight''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s sequels, ''[[New Moon (2009 film)|New Moon]]''<ref>{{cite web | author=Larry Carroll | title=Exclusive: Is Bella's Dad Being Cut Out of 'Twilight' Sequel? We've Got the Scoop! | url=http://moviesblog.mtv.com/2009/04/15/exclusive-is-bellas-dad-being-cut-out-of-twilight-sequel-weve-got-the-scoop/ | publisher=MTV | date=2009=04-15 | accessdate=April 19, 2009 }}</ref> and ''[[Eclipse (2010 film)|Eclipse]]''.
Burke is one of the "famous faces" on the [[online poker]] website [[Hollywood Poker]], which is run in conjunction with [[Ongame Network]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Billy Burke Biography|url=https://member.hollywoodpoker.com/green-room/celebrity-poker/biographies/billy-burke.html | accessdate=September 7, 2007 }}</ref> In February 2010, Burke was cast as Jonah King, the primary antagonist featured in the thriller ''[[Drive Angry]]'',<ref>[http://www.moviehole.net/201023600-exclusive-bellas-dad-drives-angry Exclusive : Bella's Dad Drive's Angry]</ref> which was directed by [[Patrick Lussier]]<ref>[http://www.bloody-disgusting.com/news/20972 SD Comic-Con '10: First Official Stills from 'Drive Angry 3D'!]</ref> and co-starred [[Amber Heard]], [[Nicolas Cage]], and [[William Fichtner]].<ref>[http://www.dreadcentral.com/news/35985/twilights-billy-burke-next-drive-angry Twilight's Billy Burke Next to Drive Angry]</ref> It was released on February 25, 2011.
As of July 2010, Burke appears in the [[TNT (TV channel)|TNT]] drama series ''[[Rizzoli & Isles]]''.<ref name=pr01-21-10>{{Cite press release|url=http://turner.tekgroup.com/article_display.cfm?article_id=4931|title=TNT Aggressively Expands Original Programming Slate by Greenlighting Three New Original Series|publisher=[[Turner Broadcasting System]]|date=January 21, 2010|accessdate=June 20, 2010}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.multichannel.com/article/452878-2010_Cable_Upfronts_TNT_Leverages_Sundays_For_Originals.php| title=2010 Cable Upfronts: TNT Leverages Sundays For Originals|last=Reynolds|first=Mike|date=May 19, 2010|work=[[Multichannel News]]|publisher=NewBay Media|accessdate=June 21, 2010}}</ref>
Burke is married to actress Pollyanna Rose; they have a daughter named Bluesy LaRue Burke.<ref>http://moviesblog.mtv.com/2009/11/13/twilight-star-billy-burke-to-join-his-wife-and-daughter-in-luster/</ref><ref>http://www.mtv.com/news/articles/1625660/billy-burke-hopes-his-daughter-just-like-bella-swan.jhtml</ref>
